## Feature summary (web, SideFX reference)

- Source: https://www.sidefx.com/docs/houdini/nodes/cop/grunge_moisture.html
- Summary (EN): Grunge Moisture procedurally generates a spotted pattern resembling damp, sponge-like texture. It works well as a mask or as a building block for textures such as sponge-painted surfaces or condensation on glass.
- Résumé (FR) : Grunge Moisture produit un motif de taches humides, proche d'une éponge, utilisable en masque pour une surface peinte à l'éponge ou de la condensation sur verre.

- Inputs meaning: ["size_ref: representative layer that sets the output size and metadata"]

- Key parameters: ["Range: Amplitude scales values before Center, Center offsets them, Mask Contrast adjusts contrast", "Pattern: Element Size, Offset, Tile Size", "Detail: visibility of the spots set by Density", "Distort: directional distortion, which can produce cellular looks", "Density: amount of spots, of various sizes at higher values", "Sharpen: sharpens or softens the spots", "Seed: changes the random result while keeping the same look", "Post Processing, applied in order: Fold, Complement, Bias, Gain, Gamma, Contrast, Clamp Minimum, Clamp Maximum"]

- Caveats: ["Output can be negative or above 1; the page recommends the Clamp options", "Fold has no visible effect when all values are positive", "Complement assumes values in the 0 to 1 range", "Post-processing Contrast differs from Noise Contrast", "Tile Size should match the aspect ratio of non-square images"]

